# Unanchored rather than `/target/`, and deliberately kept that way. It was
# first written to catch the per-crate `abi/target/`, `env/target/` and the
# rest, which `xtask coverage` used to scatter profiles into because it set a
# *relative* `LLVM_PROFILE_FILE` — E0-B17 fixed the cause. The pattern stays
# because a stray build directory is still not a source, and an ignore rule
# that only worked by accident is worth keeping on purpose.
target/

# `.cargo/config.toml` is tracked, and has to be: it carries the `xtask` alias
# and the kernel's link flags, so `cargo xtask` does not exist in a checkout
# without it. Only a CARGO_HOME vendored under this directory is ignored — the
# container puts its own at /opt/cargo, so nothing in the tree writes here.
/.cargo/registry/
/.cargo/git/

*.iso
*.img
/claims/*.local.jsonl

# CI writes these; they are reports, not sources.
/detect.txt
/scan.md

# Team settings are tracked; personal ones are not. .claude/README.md says so.
/.claude/settings.local.json
